### Page 1 of 2

```text
RESOLUTION NO. __________

ENTITLED: "A RESOLUTION EXPRESSING THE INTENT OF THE GOVERNING
BODY, REPEALING AND REPLACING RESOLUTION NO. 6127
GOVERNING THE CREATION AND ADMINISTRATION OF THE
INNOVATION AND ENTREPRENEUR ADVISORY COUNCIL."

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming is committed to supporting the success and
strength of the local and state economy and encourages the efforts of local businesses;

WHEREAS, local businesses are the backbone of our economy and are integral to the
growth and longevity of the community;

WHEREAS, in recognition of this fact, on February 22, 2021, the Governing Body adopted
Resolution No. 6127, creating the Innovations and Entrepreneur Advisory Council;

WHEREAS, the Governing Body still believes that in order to attract, retain and support
startup businesses and entrepreneurs, solutions to issues critical to driving the innovation economy
need to be identified and implemented, including enabling entrepreneurs to successfully access
and develop a skilled, globally competitive workforce;

WHEREAS, since the creation of this advisory council, the Governing Body has
determined that certain modifications to the composition and administration of the council should
be made in the interest of efficiency, efficacy and transparency;

WHEREAS, the Governing Body wishes to reconstitute and reauthorize the Innovations
and Entrepreneur Advisory Council, originally created by Resolution No. 6127, so that it may
continue to serve as a vehicle for ongoing dialogue regarding entrepreneurship and workforce
development in the community, and empower the community so that entrepreneurs can launch
companies, scale technology and create the jobs of tomorrow;

WHEREAS, the membership of the Innovations and Entrepreneur Advisory Council shall
now be comprised of nine (9) members, of which seven (7) members shall be appointed by the
Mayor and who shall possess professional experience in one (1) or more of the following fields:
finance, marketing or advertising, building or construction, or information technology;

WHEREAS, the remaining two (2) members of the nine (9) member council shall consist
of one (1) at-large representative who shall be a resident of the city of Cheyenne to be nominated
by the Mayor and approved by the Governing Body and one (1) member of the Governing Body
of the City of Cheyenne who shall be appointed by City Council President;

WHEREAS, the Governing Body wishes that the Mayor appoint the necessary members
of the Innovations and Entrepreneur Advisory Council, as reconstituted herein, as soon as possible
subject to confirmation by the City Council as provided by Section 2.08.010 of the city code;

9:55 am, Oct 21, 2024
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
Page 2 of 2
WHEREAS, in the interest of efficiency and transparency, the Governing Body intends for
the newly reconstituted council to draft and approve by-laws specifying council process and
procedures, including provisions governing executive officers, council meetings and minutes, and
conflicts of interest and necessary disclosures; and

WHEREAS, in order to stay apprised of and engaged with the important work of the
Innovations and Entrepreneur Advisory Council, the Governing Body intends for the council to
annually report to the Governing Body on its work, progress and accomplishments over the
previous fiscal year, and its more immediate goals and objective moving forward.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY
OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that Resolution No. 6127 (Feb. 22, 2021), is hereby repealed and
replaced or otherwise superseded and that the Entrepreneur Advisory Council is reconstituted and
reauthorized as provided herein;

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, the Entrepreneur Advisory Council shall draft and adopt
by-laws as stated herein, specifying how the council shall be governed, which by-laws shall be
adopted not less than six (6) months after the date that the last of any and all currently vacant
positions on the council have been filled; and

BE IT FINALLY RESOLVED, that the Innovations and Entrepreneur Advisory Council
shall annually report to the Governing Body as stated herein by June 30 of each fiscal year.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED this _______ day of _____________________,
2024.

__________________________________________
Patrick Collins, Mayor

(SEAL)

ATTEST:

____________________________________
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
```
